How we researched and tested

We started by researching dozens of ski boot bags and ski boot backpacks, comparing product specs, design features, media reviews, and user feedback. From there, we narrowed the field to the most promising options to test ourselves.

We spent more than a year testing ski boot bags on short and long ski road trips, backcountry outings, and international travel, including a ski trip to Japan.

During testing, we evaluated protection, organization, durability, carry comfort, capacity, and weather resistance. We also looked at details such as padding and rigidity around boots, helmets, and goggles; boot-specific compartments; straps and carry systems; and how well each bag handled snow, slush, parking lots, trailheads, and other real-world travel conditions.

We also considered how easily wet gear could be separated from dry gear and whether the bags had useful ventilation or drainage features after a day on the slopes.

